### Page 1 of 3

```text
PUBLIC SERVICES COMMITTEE
MINUTES
A meeting of the Public Services Committee was held on Monday, May 5, 2025, in Council
Chambers and via electronic meeting, starting at 12:00 p.m. Those in attendance were as follows:
COMMITTEE MEMBERS:
Tom Segrave, Chairman; Dr. Michelle Aldrich: Dr. Kathy
Emmons and Jeff White (via Zoom).
AGENDA ITEMS
10.
ORDINANCE —3 READING
— Repealing Chapter 12.28, Downtown Graffiti Abatement
Pilol Program of Title 12, Streets, Sidewalks and Public Places, of the Municipal Code of
the City of Cheyenne. Wyoming.
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 3fh and final reading, seconded by Dr. Emmons. Motion carried
by unanimous voice vote.
Charles Bloom, Planning & Development Department Director, provided a staff report and advised
that no changes have been made since 2” reading. Committee member Aldrich confirmed the sun
set date for the pilot program was in 2020,
11.
ORDINANCE —2 READING— Amending Sections 1.4.3, 1.4.4, and 5.7.2 of the Unified
Development Code to amend specific uses allowed as Home Occupations and add
clarifying definitions. (SPONSORS
— MR. MOODY AND MR. SEGRAVE)
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on Vd reading, seconded by Dr. Emmons. Dr. Aldrich moved to
amend to strike all references in the proposed ordinance to Massage Parlors; to strike from section
5.7.2(j) number (4) Animal grooming salons (only) and number (5) Body piercing/body art/tattoo
art (in its entirety) as exclusions to home occupations; and to strike the language in 5.7.2(e)
allowing for one vehicle and trailer associated with the business to be in the public right-of-way.
seconded by Dr. Emmons. Motion to amend carried by unanimous voice vote. Main motion, as
amended carried by unanimous voice vote.
Connor White, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report and provided an
overview of the proposed changes. All committee members commented on the item as did Ward
Ill Councilman and sponsor of the item. Mark Moody.
12.
RESOLUTION
— Granting an exception to the ‘201 Agreement’ for the owner of the
property located south of High Plains Road and west of South Greeley Highway, between
Robert Avenue and Dayshia Lane. (POSTPONED FROM APRIL 28, 2025)
The item died due to the lack of a motion.
```

### Page 2 of 3

```text
Charles Bloom, Planning & Development Department Director, provided a staff report and advised
additional information would be available at the upcoming governing body meeting on May 12,
2025.
17.
RESOLUTION
— Expressing the support of the Governing Body for acceptance of real
property from Sloan Lake, LLC. (SPONSOR - MR. SEGRAVE)
Dr. Emmons moved to adopt, seconded by Mr. White. Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
Jean Shrednik. Parks & Greenway Planner, provided a staff report and Tom Cobb. City Engineer,
provided additional information related to the development and installation of sidewalk to the area.
Committee members Aldrich and Emmons commented on the item.
18.
RESOLUTION
— Finding and declaring certain areas within the City of Cheyenne as blight
and authorizing the redevelopment thereof in accordance with Wyoming Statute § 15-9-
106. (SPONSOR—MR. SEGRAVE)
Dr. Aldrich moved to adopt, seconded by Dr. Emmons. Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
Brandon Gilchrist, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report. Charles Bloom,
Planning & Development Department Director, provided information related to the collection of
tax increment funding (TIF) and the ongoing discussion with the county. Chairman Segrave and
all committee members commented on the item. Public comment was made by Brandon Swain.
19.
RESOLUTION
— Certifying compliance with Wyoming Statute § 15-1-402 for the City-
initiated annexation of various tracts of land completely surrounded by current city limits
situate in northeast Cheyenne generally located north Dell Range Boulevard, west and east
of Ridge Road, and south of Storey Boulevard. (SPONSOR
— MR. SEGRAVE)
Dr. Aldrich moved to adopt, seconded by Dr. Emmons. Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
Connor White, Planning & Development Department. provided a staff report and provided the
timelinc for the proposed annexations. Committee members Aldrich and Emmons commented on
the item.
20.
RESOLUTION
— Certifying and adopting the Belvoir Ranch Master Plan. (SPONSOR
—
MR. SEGRAVE)
Dr. Aldrich moved to adopt, seconded by Mr. White. Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
Connor White, Planning & Development Department. provided a staff report and Mark
Christenson. AVI P.C., provided additional information regarding the creation of the updated plan
noting one recommendation from the Planning Commission to include a goal to work with Board
of Public Utilities to include water resource policies on the ranch.
Committee member Aldrich
commented on the item and verified the Planning Commission’s recommendation would be
included in the final version of the master plan.
```

